  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## <i class=\"fa-solid fa-sparkles\"></i> Start Here <i class=\"fa-solid fa-sparkles\"></i>\r\n\r\nWelcome to **Web Lab**! You'll be using this editor and an AI assistant to build websites.\r\n\r\nWe're starting with a practice page about Otters. You'll get to create your own custom webpage in the next level, but for now, follow the steps below (be sure to scroll down!) to learn how to interact with AI tutor.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. **Highlight** an example prompt from the center panel and select **\"Add to AI Tutor Chat\"**\r\n\r\n![](https://images.code.org/c487d1200b442fb27ba266228689eddf-image-1776372888974.png)\r\n\r\n2. In the chat box below, tell AI Tutor to make that change to the webpage (ex: \"Make this update to the otter website\")\r\n3. **Review and Accept:** Check the preview on the right. If it looks good, click **\"Accept\"** and write a short summary of the change.\r\n\r\n> **Tip:** Click **\"Hide Instructions\"** to give more room to AI Tutor.\r\n\r\nOnce AI tutor has made a change to the webpage, click **Continue**.",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "true",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "predict_settings": {
      "isPredictLevel": false,
      "solution": "",
      "questionType": "freeResponse",
      "placeholderText": "",
      "multipleChoiceOptions": [
        ""
      ],
      "freeResponseHeight": 50,
      "codeEditableAfterSubmit": false
    },
    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "buildCSS",
        "buildHTML"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "explainCode": "- Limit responses to just HTML. Do not mention CSS or Javascript.",
        "buildCSS": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do NOT use separate file name. Put all css in a `<style>` tag in the head of the index.html file\n- You should generate both HTML and CSS at the same time\n- Keep explanations sparse and simple, acknowledging the work that has been done. Do NOT list specific HTML tags or CSS rules that have been changed. Do NOT explain how HTML or CSS works.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! You've already made a change to the page. Go ahead and click Continue to move on!'",
        "buildHTML": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Do NOT link a style.css file\n- Do NOT use IDs or class on elements\n- Do NOT generate links or buttons\n- Keep explanations sparse and simple, acknowledging the work that has been done. Do NOT list specific HTML tags or CSS rules that have been changed. Do NOT explain how HTML or CSS works.\n- If the student has already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! You've already made a change to the page. Go ahead and click Continue to move on!'"
      }
    },
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n\n<head>\n    <title>All About Otters!</title>\n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Open Sans', sans-serif;\n            color: #333333;\n            margin: 0;\n            line-height: 1.6;\n        }\n\n        header, footer {\n            background-color: #f0f8ff;\n            padding: 1rem;\n            text-align: center;\n            border: 2px solid #a7d9f7;\n            color: #005f99;\n        }\n\n        main {\n            padding: 1rem;\n            max-width: 960px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n        }\n\n        section {\n            margin-bottom: 1rem;\n            padding: 1rem;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n        }\n\n        #otter-facts {\n            background-color: #fff5e1;\n            border: 3px solid #ffd700;\n            font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;\n            color: #8b4513;\n        }\n\n        #otter-swimmers {\n            background-color: #e0f8e0;\n            border: 3px solid #8bc34a;\n            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;\n            color: #33691e;\n        }\n\n        #otter-locations {\n            background-color: #ffe0b2;\n            border: 3px solid #ff9800;\n            font-family: 'Merriweather', serif;\n            color: #e65100;\n        }\n\n        #otter-predators {\n            background-color: #ffcccc;\n            border-color: #cc0000;\n            font-family: 'Verdana', sans-serif;\n            color: #660000;\n        }\n\n        .two-column-layout {\n            display: flex;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            gap: 1rem;\n        }\n\n        .two-column-layout section {\n            flex: 1;\n            min-width: 300px;\n        }\n\n        img {\n            max-width: 100%;\n            height: auto;\n            border-radius: 15px;\n            border: 5px solid #a7d9f7;\n        }\n\n        h1 {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        #image-credit {\n            font-size: 10px;\n            color: #6699bb;\n        }\n\n        hr#otter-divider {\n            border: 3px dashed #a7d9f7;\n            background-color: transparent;\n            color: #a7d9f7;\n        }\n\n    </style>\n</head>\n\n<body>\n    <header>\n      <h1>Welcome to the Otter Zone!</h1>\n    </header>\n\n    <main>\n      <div class=\"two-column-layout\">\n        <section id=\"otter-facts\">\n          <h2>Cool Otter Facts!</h2>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Did you know otters hold hands when they sleep so they don't drift apart? Awww!</li>\n            <li>They can also hold their breath for a loooong time underwater!</li>\n          </ul>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"otter-swimmers\">\n          <h2>Otterly Amazing Swimmers!</h2>\n          <p>Otters are super speedy in the water! They use their powerful tails and webbed feet to zoom around.</p>\n          <p>They can dive deep to find yummy snacks like fish and crabs.</p>\n        </section>\n      </div>\n\n      <hr id=\"otter-divider\">\n\n      <section id=\"otter-locations\">\n        <h2>Where in the World are Otters?</h2>\n        <p>You can find different kinds of otters all over the globe, from chilly Alaska to sunny Brazil.</p>\n        <p>Some live in rivers, some in coasts, and some even in the open ocean!</p>\n      </section>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n      <p>Thanks for visiting the otter-tastic website!</p>\n    </footer>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>\n",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
