    "name_suffix": "_launch",
    "offer_browser_tts": "true",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** This level is about getting used to the Web Lab editor, and using a common \"Add to AI tutor\" workflow that continues throughout this progression. Students should leave knowing how to highlight code, send it to AI Tutor, and make a decision about the output.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What did you highlight and send to AI Tutor? What did it do?\"  \r\n- \"Did you accept the change? Why or why not?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may click Accept without looking at the preview \\- redirect them: \"before you accept, check the preview. Does it look the way you expected?\"  \r\n- Students may not know what to write in the chat after highlighting \\- suggest they describe what they want to happen: \"just tell AI Tutor to make the change you highlighted\"  \r\n- Students may try to make many changes at once or continue to iterate on this page \\- encourage them to just make one change and continue",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
